From 8eb8656ac77723dbd89e9f0973da1d6b520d2a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:39:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] trans/minicargo: a `staticlib` carries the `static=` native
 archives of its crate graph

newsboat 2.45 (net/newsboat, upstream Portfile: PortGroup rust + makefile) links its Rust half as just
target/<triple>/release/libnewsboat.a (libnewsboat-ffi, `crate-type = ["staticlib"]`, `[lib] name = "newsboat"`).
Its cxx bridge code is C++ that the build scripts compile into archives: cxx-build in libnewsboat-ffi's build.rs
(`cargo:rustc-link-lib=static=libnewsboat-ffi-<module>`, 16 of them) and cc in cxx's (`static=cxxbridge1`). rustc
copies the members of such archives into the staticlib (`static` = `+bundle` by default); mrustc's staticlib (0147)
only listed native libraries in `lib<name>.a.libs`, and minicargo passed every library on as a bare name, so the C++
link of newsboat would lack the bridge functions. (minicargo even recorded a missing kind as "static", and stopped
with "TODO: rustc-link-lib static:-bundle" on a modifier, which cc prints when asked to.)

- minicargo: `rustc-link-lib` takes `KIND[:MODIFIERS]=NAME`; an explicit `static` goes to mrustc as
  `-l static=NAME` (`-l static:-bundle=NAME` with `-bundle`), no kind / `dylib` stay bare names, `framework=` as before.
- expand: `#[link(kind = "static")]` is encoded the same way (the `framework=` precedent), `modifiers` kept.
- C backend: library names are parsed (`NativeLib::parse`); a `staticlib` resolves each bundled `static=` library of
  the crate and of every dependency to `lib<name>.a` (the crate's own search directories, then this crate's: std's
  `static=emutls`/`static=MacportsLegacySupport` come from build_std.txt), extracts its object members (System V/GNU
  and BSD `ar` formats, symbol tables skipped; written as `<lib>-<n>-<member>` in `<out>.bundle/`, so same-named
  members don't collide) and adds them to the archive. Unbundled ones stay in `.libs`; a missing or unreadable
  archive is a warning and stays there too. Executables and dylibs link exactly as before (the kind is stripped).

No rlib format change (the kind travels in the library name, like `framework=`). Rlibs built before carry bare
names, so only crates built after this are bundled; the mrustc port's own libstd build then records std's
`static=MacportsLegacySupport`/`static=emutls` (build_std.txt), which every staticlib then carries. An archive that
can't be read (a universal one, a GNU thin archive) is a warning and goes to `.libs` as its path.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)
